  "term": "sensory test",
  "definition": "A sensory test is a way of measuring how well a person detects different kinds of sensation, such as temperature or vibration. In this source, it refers to a simplified form of quantitative sensory testing used to track changes in sensory nerve function and possible neuropathy.",
